I’ll inspect the measurement metadata, pattern, and the reusable refinement helpers first. Then I’ll build a chemically plausible phase inventory, refine candidates in GSAS-II, challenge alternatives against the residual, and export every deliverable from the final saved project.

The chemistry points first to lead tungstate formation, but the unknown phase count means I’m treating unreacted oxides and Pb–W–O intermediates as live candidates rather than assuming a single product. I’m now enumerating database records and checking the observed peak families before selecting structures.

Three coherent phase signatures are already visible after accounting for an approximately +0.4° angular offset: scheelite PbWO₄, monoclinic WO₃, and tetragonal Pb₃O₄. Each has distinctive low- and mid-angle families, so I’m now comparing alternate records/polymorphs under the same offset/profile assumptions before committing to the inventory.

