With polarization fixed at 1.0, the coordinate test independently made the same four accept/reject decisions and retained all contact checks. The endpoint costs only 0.00047 Rwp percentage point versus the unconstrained nuisance fit, so the fit quality is effectively unchanged while the model is now physically bounded.

The exact-final watch-list replay confirms massicot: removing it worsens Rwp from 3.193% to 4.563%, while tetragonal litharge drives its scale to the numerical floor (~10⁻¹²). The retained massicot reflections form coherent families from about 29.5° through 98.1°, so this is not a single-peak assignment.

